<title>INDIA: India's M3 money supply growth steady at 16.2 pct.</title>
<headline>India's M3 money supply growth steady at 16.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's year-on-year M3 money supply growth was 16.2 percent on December 20, unchanged from the previous fortnight, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.  </p>
<p>		   M3 MONEY SUPPLY GROWTH (yr-on-yr in pct)</p>
<p>		   Dec 20, 1996   Dec 6, 1996  Dec 22, 1995</p>
<p>		   16.2	     16.2	    14.3</p>
<p>Money supply was 6,589.30 billion rupees on December 20 compared to 6,580.49 billion rupees on December 6, 1996 and 5,647.78 billion on December 22, 1995, the RBI said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
